                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "239361807",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198062506049",
                            "num_reviews": 997,
                            "playtime_forever": 1510,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 1510,
                            "playtime_at_review": 1510,
                            "last_played": 1793797395
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I also think it's worth mentioning that Breach has an interesting concept, essentially taking the hacking mechanics and turning them into a standalone first person action and stealth experience. There are some enjoyable ideas here, with different servers, enemy placements, equipment and challenges to work through. Unfortunately, the repetitive level layouts and progression systems can wear thin, and the monetisation only makes the experience more frustrating. It's a shame because there's a decent little game buried underneath these decisions, but I don't think free to play suits these singleplayer experiences at all. When you also take in the repetitive environments, occasionally frustrating enemy AI and the feeling that an interesting concept wasn't executed particularly well. Its nice that its free with its interesting concept albeit questionable design. I can't recommend supporting this kind of monetisation, even if the game itself costs nothing.",
